    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Livonia is a village in eastern Putnam County, Missouri, United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livonia%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s plat was laid out in May 1859 by Absalom Grogan, who also served as its first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livonia%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After Grogan’s death, the post office moved to Joseph Martin’s farm about three miles north of the original plat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livonia%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "On July 26, 2011, the United States Postal Service announced plans to permanently close Livonia’s post office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livonia%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Livonia sits on Missouri Route N just north of U.S. Route 136 in southeastern Grant Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livonia%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Chariton River marks the Putnam‑Schuyler county line just east of Livonia, separating the two counties.",
